# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the linux-clang-asan preset (ADR 0008).
#
# ngspice leaks a little on every load, which nothing short of ending the process gives back
# (ADR 0002). Every such leak is allocated by ngspice's own allocator, tmalloc, or by the OpenMP
# runtime it loads. Matching on tmalloc rather than on libngspice.so keeps Proton's own leaks
# visible: Proton's data callback runs with ngspice's frames on its stack, but never allocates
# through tmalloc.
leak:tmalloc
leak:libgomp.so
